## Reached at
  The target is an OSClass tree served by a PHP 7.4 Apache instance whose
  document root is /var/www/html, listening on port 80 of the application
  container. Callers resolve a base URL as

      BASE_URL = os.environ.get("TARGET_URL", "http://localhost")

  and reach two PHP scripts by ordinary HTTP GET through that server:

      GET {BASE_URL}/oc-content/themes/modern/combine.php
      GET {BASE_URL}/oc-includes/osclass/gui/combine.php

  Both files are project-owned copies of the same combiner script shipped
  inside the OSClass tree staged by the image build; the two copies sit in the
  two directories above and each is reached by the callers, so the
  reconstructed code must land at both of these paths as served by this web
  server — not in another server, tool, helper, or wrapper. The Apache/PHP
  runtime and the MySQL service it waits on are pre-existing system
  components, not part of the reconstructed code. Static assets served from
  the same two directories (style.css, tabs.css, js/global.js) belong to the
  existing tree.

## Must provide
  /oc-content/themes/modern/combine.php   PHP script under the docroot, served
                                          by the web server, answering HTTP GET
  /oc-includes/osclass/gui/combine.php    second copy of the same script, same
                                          HTTP GET interface
  Both scripts are reached through the query parameters "type" and "files" on
  GET; both copies carry the same interface.

## Called as
  Both entrypoints are called identically; {base} is one of the two directories
  above. The caller writes:

      requests.get(BASE_URL + base + "/combine.php",
                   params={"type": <type>, "files": <files>},
                   headers=PLAIN_HEADERS)

  which arrives at the script as:

      GET {base}/combine.php?type=<type>&files=<files>

  type     — URL query parameter named "type"; a string. Functional callers
             pass "css" or "js".
  files    — URL query parameter named "files"; a string: one relative path,
             or several relative paths separated by commas. Functional callers
             pass "style.css", "js/global.js", and "style.css,tabs.css".
  Headers  — the callers send, on every request:
                 User-Agent: Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 5.0
                 Accept-Encoding: identity
             A follow-up request to the same URL may additionally carry an
             If-None-Match request header whose value is a string.

## Setup required
  - The Apache server of the application container must already be answering
    at TARGET_URL (default http://localhost) before the calls land; the
    container entrypoint waits for the MySQL service (MYSQL_HOST=db) and then
    keeps apache2-foreground running under a restart loop.
  - The docroot is /var/www/html and the two scripts are reached through the
    server'"'"'s normal PHP dispatch under that docroot (mod_rewrite enabled,
    AllowOverride All); no further routing or registration stands between the
    URL and the script files.
  - Callers run as root inside the same container the requests are made
    against, and poll the base URL until it answers before issuing requests.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side is a pytest process that uses the requests library to issue
