- **Outputs and errors:** A request without `path` terminates via the retained `show_tips` with a parameter-error message. When the configuration supplies an `apiKey`: the request terminates with a token-error message unless the request'"'"'s `token` equals the md5 digest of the configured apiKey concatenated with the request'"'"'s `path` value and the `timeTo` value coerced to an integer (empty string when absent); then, when `timeTo` is non-empty and is less than or equal to the current time, the request terminates with an expiry message. With no `apiKey`, the `token` and `timeTo` inputs have no effect and the request proceeds. On success the rendered `view.html` from this class'"'"'s template directory is the HTTP response body.
