- **Observable behavior:** The zipfile module'"'"'s xUpdate: applies DELETE, INSERT, REPLACE, and UPDATE (including renames) to the write transaction'"'"'s in-memory entry list; new entry bytes are appended to the archive file immediately, and directory changes accumulate for commit.
- **Inputs:** WITHOUT ROWID xUpdate array: `apVal[0]` NULL means insert, else the text name of the entry to delete/update; `nVal==1` means delete; with `nVal>1`, `apVal[1]` is the new name and `apVal[2..8]` are the new name, mode, mtime, sz, rawdata, data, method values. `pRowid` is unused.
- **Outputs and errors:** SQLITE_OK on success (including an IGNORE-policy no-op); SQLITE_CONSTRAINT with a table error message when a write violates a column constraint — non-NULL sz or rawdata, a method other than 0, 8, or NULL, a duplicate name under the default conflict policy, and mode-decoding failures are reported this way; SQLITE_NOMEM; begin/append/deflate errors propagate.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Begins the write transaction through the surrounding begin when none is open. New entry: fixed header fields, compression method, DOS plus unix mtime, CRC-32 of the uncompressed data, sizes, mode shifted into the external attributes, offset at the current archive size; the local header plus stored or deflated bytes are appended to the archive; the entry joins the directory list at the replaced entry'"'"'s position, else the end. Directory paths gain a trailing `/`. Method NULL deflates only when smaller; method 8 always. Replaced/removed entries are unlinked, and open cursors positioned on them advance past.
- **Required sequencing and state:** begin → locate the old entry (path match ignoring trailing `/`) → sz/rawdata NULL checks → data/method handling → mode decoding → name/mtime → directory slash normalization → duplicate-policy check (inserts and renames only) → append and list insertion → unlink old entries. The check order decides which error is reported.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained: the range spans one complete function declaration; the retained text above ends with a comment and the retained text below begins the next function. The restored definition must nonetheless precede the retained `zipfileModule` initializer further down, which resolves the name `zipfileUpdate`.
